From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mxreyer <236478497+mxreyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winograd: optional fp16 inner loop (DLPRIM_CONV_FP16=1)

Behind an environment variable, off by default: the three Winograd kernels
convert their tiles to half on the way into LDS and run the register-tile
GEMM as half2 mad with half accumulation over one work-group's K slice
(packed v_pk_fma_f16, twice the fp32 rate on RDNA). Tensors in global
memory stay fp32; the backward-filter split-K target is raised (16 per CU,
cap 64) so the fp16 sums stay short, which halves the dW error.

On an AMD gfx1013: forward 15.0 -> 8.9 ms, backward-data 16.0 -> 10.2,
backward-filter 19.4 -> 12.4 per ResNet-9 step, 2,055 -> 2,987 img/s.
Y/dX/dW within ~0.5% of fp32, about 10x looser than TF32, hence opt-in.
A variant with fp32 accumulation via v_fma_mix_f32 was measured too:
TF32-class accuracy but slower than plain fp32 on this chip.

The LDS-residency rule from the previous patch is told about the half-sized
tiles: with LTYPE half a padded work-group is 20 KiB, two of them fit, and
the padding stays. Measured either way in fp16 mode, 2,889-2,901 img/s.
